    {
      "id": "E9GrnbOxQ05KNs_A4CbWl",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4916.031746031743,
      "y": -1979.988095238095,
      "width": 2062.466666666664,
      "height": 449.99999999999966,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a5",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1013022340,
      "version": 1333,
      "versionNonce": 2090243811,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "yyfv2L5AojZOWpPZGyi0G",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1790448438577,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "A runtime structure/state that keeps track of the information JavaScript needs while executing a particular piece\nof code.\n\nThere are mainly 3 types:\n1. Global Execution Context :- Created when the JavaScript program starts executing.\n2. Function Execution Context :- Created every time a function is called.\n3. Eval Execution Context : -Created when code inside eval() is executed. We generally don't use eval(), so we don't\nneed to worry about this for now.\n\nHow it look like :-",
      "fontSize": 35.99999999999997,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "A runtime structure/state that keeps track of the information JavaScript needs while executing a particular piece of code.\n\nThere are mainly 3 types:\n1. Global Execution Context :- Created when the JavaScript program starts executing.\n2. Function Execution Context :- Created every time a function is called.\n3. Eval Execution Context : -Created when code inside eval() is executed. We generally don't use eval(), so we don't need to worry about this for now.\n\nHow it look like :-",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "NYEhMAQW8LHnuwcigXAgh",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4923.232007276546,
      "y": -1467.1297424961938,
      "width": 1451.3373767315302,
      "height": 809.9999999999993,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a5G",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1455516419,
      "version": 1493,
      "versionNonce": 1591275949,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "yyfv2L5AojZOWpPZGyi0G",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1790452686147,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Think :- \"Where and how is this code currently executing?\"\n\n\"Where\" refers to the environment and scope in which the code is executing.\n\nFor example, global code has access to the global environment, while code running\ninside a function has its own environment containing things like its parameters\nand locally declared variables.\n\n\"How\" refers to the rules and runtime information JavaScript uses to execute the\ncode.\n\nFor example:\n\nWhat does \"this\" refer to?\nWhat variables/bindings are available?\nWhere should JavaScript look when resolving a variable?\nWhat is the function's outer lexical environment?\nHow are declarations initialized?",
      "fontSize": 35.99999999999997,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Think :- \"Where and how is this code currently executing?\"\n\n\"Where\" refers to the environment and scope in which the code is executing.\n\nFor example, global code has access to the global environment, while code running inside a function has its own environment containing things like its parameters and locally declared variables.\n\n\"How\" refers to the rules and runtime information JavaScript uses to execute the code.\n\nFor example:\n\nWhat does \"this\" refer to?\nWhat variables/bindings are available?\nWhere should JavaScript look when resolving a variable?\nWhat is the function's outer lexical environment?\nHow are declarations initialized?",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "c8snNs9dgLIuhnCmaEK06",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4934.762486772484,
      "y": 93.01190476190527,
      "width": 2051.005185185182,
      "height": 318.4999999999996,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a5V",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 877818044,
      "version": 1651,
      "versionNonce": 795521037,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "MA1_VIzckhHYjxle0MR5O",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1790446370581,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Every time a function is called, JavaScript creates a function execution context.\nWhere does JavaScript keep track of those execution contexts while they are running? That's where the Call Stack\ncomes in. ( Last In, First Out )\n\nJavaScript is generally single-threaded.\nImp :- Meaning, one JavaScript execution thread has one call stack and can execute one piece of JavaScript at a\ntime. as it runs line by line",
      "fontSize": 36.399999999999956,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Every time a function is called, JavaScript creates a function execution context.\nWhere does JavaScript keep track of those execution contexts while they are running? That's where the Call Stack comes in. ( Last In, First Out )\n\nJavaScript is generally single-threaded.\nImp :- Meaning, one JavaScript execution thread has one call stack and can execute one piece of JavaScript at a time. as it runs line by line",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "q1nwnTctczQ44-ty7vaFR",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 10394.762486772484,
      "y": -2116.9880952380945,
      "width": 1327.5414781571471,
      "height": 363.99999999999955,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a5Z",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2018862704,
      "version": 1819,
      "versionNonce": 1833142829,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790445501099,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "\"Web APIs are features provided by the browser, not by JavaScript itself.\"\n\nDon't think:\"Web API = asynchronous.\"That's not necessarily true.\ndocument.querySelector(\"#box\");\nDOM APIs are Web APIs, but this operation is synchronous.\n\nSome Web APIs involve asynchronous operations, and those operations\neventually interact with Tasks/Microtasks.",
      "fontSize": 36.399999999999956,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "\"Web APIs are features provided by the browser, not by JavaScript itself.\"\n\nDon't think:\"Web API = asynchronous.\"That's not necessarily true.\ndocument.querySelector(\"#box\");\nDOM APIs are Web APIs, but this operation is synchronous.\n\nSome Web APIs involve asynchronous operations, and those operations eventually interact with Tasks/Microtasks.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "WD_0DyUtJXFX9k84bFHxW",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 10391.128905366882,
      "y": -951.3020471415421,
      "width": 1327.5414781571471,
      "height": 818.999999999999,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a5b",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1977893008,
      "version": 2411,
      "versionNonce": 973847693,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790445501099,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Now Js start execution first it send log to the stack and print the\noutput then there is turn of setTimeout as it is a webAPI now this tell\nto browser \"Start a timer for this callback\". and js do not wait here it\ncontinues and print the c\nNow setTimeout do not directly go into the call stack when the 0ms get\nexpried the browser say \"Okay, this callback is now ready to run.\" and It\nputs the callback into the Task Queue.\nNow here the Event loop comes it continously asking :- \n\nIs the Call Stack empty?\n        ↓\n       YES\n        ↓\nIs there a task waiting in the Task Queue?\n        ↓\n       YES\n        ↓\nMove that task to the Call Stack",
      "fontSize": 36.399999999999956,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Now Js start execution first it send log to the stack and print the output then there is turn of setTimeout as it is a webAPI now this tell to browser \"Start a timer for this callback\". and js do not wait here it continues and print the c\nNow setTimeout do not directly go into the call stack when the 0ms get expried the browser say \"Okay, this callback is now ready to run.\" and It puts the callback into the Task Queue.\nNow here the Event loop comes it continously asking :- \n\nIs the Call Stack empty?\n        ↓\n       YES\n        ↓\nIs there a task waiting in the Task Queue?\n        ↓\n       YES\n        ↓\nMove that task to the Call Stack",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "lufHeNbIKP6lddX37Sf8h",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 10583.466720695013,
      "y": 393.154415109261,
      "width": 809.208144823815,
      "height": 45.49999999999994,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a5bV",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1707771024,
      "version": 2725,
      "versionNonce": 2011079405,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790445501099,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Microtasks have higher priority than Tasks.",
      "fontSize": 36.399999999999956,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Microtasks have higher priority than Tasks.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "7i_cQ861HR1FumUu1auAm",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 11066.800054028346,
      "y": 906.4877484425942,
      "width": 869.208144823815,
      "height": 45.49999999999994,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a5bd",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1193742960,
      "version": 2967,
      "versionNonce": 1366951587,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790445501134,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "In this example the output will be A D C and B",
      "fontSize": 36.399999999999956,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "In this example the output will be A D C and B",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
