          "id": "95Z3emARVaFShZ4WHQPNS",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1790445501099,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Structured Cloning\n\nNow Structured cloning is like JSON.stringify() + JSON.parse() which can copy the\nneasted part also. but it is more cabable than that and this is how we use it :- \nBy JSON.stringify() + JSON.parse() you can loose Date , Map , Set ,BigInt ,undefined\nstructuredClone() is specifically designed to clone many of these JavaScript data\ntypes correctly.\nFunctions cannot be structured-cloned",
      "fontSize": 36.399999999999956,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Structured Cloning\n\nNow Structured cloning is like JSON.stringify() + JSON.parse() which can copy the neasted part also. but it is more cabable than that and this is how we use it :- \nBy JSON.stringify() + JSON.parse() you can loose Date , Map , Set ,BigInt ,undefined structuredClone() is specifically designed to clone many of these JavaScript data types correctly.\nFunctions cannot be structured-cloned",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "r0DzsGSCRu9yvzLj4kCcB",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 21484.146995153347,
      "y": 2724.3855304745207,
      "width": 1989.3222419739309,
      "height": 454.99999999999943,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a5btAjl",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1625483084,
      "version": 5883,
      "versionNonce": 1540673997,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "95Z3emARVaFShZ4WHQPNS",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1790445501099,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Transferable\n\nTransferable = cut + paste \nFor example: const buffer = new ArrayBuffer(1024);\nworker.postMessage(buffer, [buffer]);\nThe second argument: [buffer] means: \"Transfer ownership of this buffer to the worker.\" After transferring, the\noriginal buffer becomes detached and can no longer be used normally.\n\nWhy is this useful?\nBecause For a large ArrayBuffer, copying can be expensive.",
      "fontSize": 36.399999999999956,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Transferable\n\nTransferable = cut + paste \nFor example: const buffer = new ArrayBuffer(1024);\nworker.postMessage(buffer, [buffer]);\nThe second argument: [buffer] means: \"Transfer ownership of this buffer to the worker.\" After transferring, the original buffer becomes detached and can no longer be used normally.\n\nWhy is this useful?\nBecause For a large ArrayBuffer, copying can be expensive.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "BT2rEnSONZCwRYMuEYMF_",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 19343.895292123583,
      "y": 3812.7258436806896,
      "width": 1996.5414781571506,
      "height": 227.49999999999972,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a5btAk",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 919772014,
      "version": 6007,
      "versionNonce": 1112739885,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "95Z3emARVaFShZ4WHQPNS",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1790445501099,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "When we send data over TCP as a stream, TCP guarantees that the bytes arrive in the correct order, but it\ndoes not guarantee how those bytes will be split into chunks when we receive them. For example, if we send 100\nbytes, we might receive them as 30 + 20 + 50 bytes or in some other chunk sizes. So we keep collecting the\nincoming chunks in a buffer until we have enough bytes to form a complete message according to our application\nprotocol, and then we interpret those bytes using something like a TypedArray or DataView",
      "fontSize": 36.399999999999956,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "When we send data over TCP as a stream, TCP guarantees that the bytes arrive in the correct order, but it does not guarantee how those bytes will be split into chunks when we receive them. For example, if we send 100 bytes, we might receive them as 30 + 20 + 50 bytes or in some other chunk sizes. So we keep collecting the incoming chunks in a buffer until we have enough bytes to form a complete message according to our application protocol, and then we interpret those bytes using something like a TypedArray or DataView",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "prLebv5up92oE83-q_0P7",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 20035.085768314057,
      "y": 4064.1544151092617,
      "width": 1322.2557638714395,
      "height": 181.99999999999977,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a5btAkG",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 259068402,
      "version": 6495,
      "versionNonce": 255492749,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "95Z3emARVaFShZ4WHQPNS",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1790445501099,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Now your application maintains a buffer until it has enough data. for e.g.\nwe need 8 bytes of data and that each part have some data like in the\nimage shown. so here we use Dataview to take data like for 1 byte we use\nunit8 , for 2 bytes we use unit16 and so on..",
      "fontSize": 36.399999999999956,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Now your application maintains a buffer until it has enough data. for e.g. we need 8 bytes of data and that each part have some data like in the image shown. so here we use Dataview to take data like for 1 byte we use unit8 , for 2 bytes we use unit16 and so on..",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "YOEmEHoIISp6GtusOGEuI",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 19195.13338736168,
      "y": -2653.1821888964655,
      "width": 1724.0414781571478,
      "height": 227.49999999999972,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a5btAl",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1706767110,
      "version": 4932,
      "versionNonce": 121940205,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "95Z3emARVaFShZ4WHQPNS",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1790445501099,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "writable : - Can the value be changed?\nenumerable :- Should the property appear during things like: Object.keys(person); If: enumerable:\nfalse then it won't appear there.\nconfigurable :- Can the property's descriptor itself be changed or can the property be deleted?\nFor example, with: configurable: true you can generally delete it: delete person.name;",
      "fontSize": 36.399999999999956,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "writable : - Can the value be changed?\nenumerable :- Should the property appear during things like: Object.keys(person); If: enumerable: false then it won't appear there.\nconfigurable :- Can the property's descriptor itself be changed or can the property be deleted? For example, with: configurable: true you can generally delete it: delete person.name;",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "_QBAaWoPbTOPuR214MPSB",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 17142.96672069501,
      "y": -2381.0122515574053,
      "width": 1744.0414781571503,
      "height": 682.4999999999991,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a5btB",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1831682502,
      "version": 4817,
      "versionNonce": 469435213,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "95Z3emARVaFShZ4WHQPNS",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1790445501099,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "An object is essentially a collection of properties. Properties has key → value\n\nPrototype\nEvery ordinary JavaScript object has an internal link to another object called its prototype.\nObjects can inherit properties and methods from other objects. \n\nQ.) if we write obj.toString() how object get this property ?\nIf the property isn't found on the object itself, JavaScript looks up the object's [[Prototype]]\nand continues searching there.\n\nQ.) where does person's prototype come from?\nJs has Object.prototype and it basically attach it with objects's [[prototype]] and you can also\nsee the prototype by Object.getPrototypeOf(obj) you cannot do person.[[Prototype]] =\nObject.prototype; // ❌ because [[Prototype]] is an internal slot, not a normal JavaScript\nproperty.",
      "fontSize": 36.399999999999956,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "An object is essentially a collection of properties. Properties has key → value\n\nPrototype\nEvery ordinary JavaScript object has an internal link to another object called its prototype. Objects can inherit properties and methods from other objects. \n\nQ.) if we write obj.toString() how object get this property ?\nIf the property isn't found on the object itself, JavaScript looks up the object's [[Prototype]] and continues searching there.\n\nQ.) where does person's prototype come from?\nJs has Object.prototype and it basically attach it with objects's [[prototype]] and you can also see the prototype by Object.getPrototypeOf(obj) you cannot do person.[[Prototype]] = Object.prototype; // ❌ because [[Prototype]] is an internal slot, not a normal JavaScript property.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "RQegsReIHvpCe3G_s1d2N",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 23902.96672069501,
      "y": -2311.0122515574058,
      "width": 1744.0414781571503,
      "height": 181.99999999999977,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a5btB6",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 20996612,
      "version": 5153,
      "versionNonce": 1370952109,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "95Z3emARVaFShZ4WHQPNS",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1790445501099,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "We already know that JavaScript normally executes on a main thread. If we perform heavy\nJavaScript work like we are doing Face detection in the frontend side the main thread is busy.\nThat can cause: UI = frozen , buttons = delayed , animation = laggy , scrolling = laggy. This is the\nproblem Web Workers solve.",
      "fontSize": 36.399999999999956,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "We already know that JavaScript normally executes on a main thread. If we perform heavy JavaScript work like we are doing Face detection in the frontend side the main thread is busy. That can cause: UI = frozen , buttons = delayed , animation = laggy , scrolling = laggy. This is the problem Web Workers solve.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "9DcSQ5MpvdgLaL1zynX29",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 23909.633387361675,
      "y": -2111.0122515574058,
      "width": 1744.0414781571503,
      "height": 90.99999999999989,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a5btB9",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2141560580,
      "version": 5304,
      "versionNonce": 1705137165,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "95Z3emARVaFShZ4WHQPNS",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1790445501099,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "A Web Worker is a separate JavaScript execution environment that runs on another thread.\nSo that means it has it own global context , call stack , Event loop and all thing.",
      "fontSize": 36.399999999999956,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "A Web Worker is a separate JavaScript execution environment that runs on another thread.\nSo that means it has it own global context , call stack , Event loop and all thing.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
