    },
    {
      "id": "c7DKM_R_GzJl3qlnCNxEj",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 8490.838947969365,
      "y": -2719.3914543802102,
      "width": 704.5995375700082,
      "height": 280.16666666666595,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a5fv",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1791677828,
      "version": 5344,
      "versionNonce": 1516460717,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790445501099,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Therefore, the arrow function's parent\nlexical scope is the global scope (window in\nbrowsers, {} or module exports in Node.js).\n\nBecause arrow functions lock this to their\nparent scope when created, this inside greet\npoints directly to the global object.",
      "fontSize": 32.019047619047534,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Therefore, the arrow function's parent lexical scope is the global scope (window in browsers, {} or module exports in Node.js).\n\nBecause arrow functions lock this to their parent scope when created, this inside greet points directly to the global object.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "9koSCxNwCNkusP0A7LGyG",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 8827.981805112222,
      "y": -3030.820025808782,
      "width": 372.8852538913774,
      "height": 283.8995097747513,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a5fw",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 45540868,
      "version": 5648,
      "versionNonce": 64847117,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790445501099,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "The arrow function asks:\n\"Who is my enclosing lexical\nscope?\"\nIt looks at the { ... } of user.\nAn object literal is not a\nfunction or a block scope; it\nis just an assignment\nexpression sitting in the\nglobal scope.",
      "fontSize": 25.235511979977897,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "The arrow function asks: \"Who is my enclosing lexical scope?\"\nIt looks at the { ... } of user. An object literal is not a function or a block scope; it is just an assignment expression sitting in the global scope.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "KjrtXbpdckAjG40A2D4Kt",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7316.200949636131,
      "y": -2923.677168665925,
      "width": 789.3385185185131,
      "height": 136.49999999999983,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a5fx",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 478005892,
      "version": 5087,
      "versionNonce": 312759149,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790445501099,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Here this refers to the person because the\nnormal function have its own this and it\nrefres to where it is created",
      "fontSize": 36.399999999999956,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Here this refers to the person because the normal function have its own this and it refres to where it is created",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "TnP2JkC7Yvfefz56iePow",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 8023.462854398034,
      "y": 308.9637733609586,
      "width": 541.6660121497126,
      "height": 366.1666666666666,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a5h",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 308442044,
      "version": 2481,
      "versionNonce": 1923106179,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790446288224,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "inside test():\n\nLook for x in test's environment.\nNot found.\nGo to the outer environment.\nFind x.\nUse 10.\n\nThis is called the scope chain.",
      "fontSize": 32.548148148148144,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "inside test():\n\nLook for x in test's environment.\nNot found.\nGo to the outer environment.\nFind x.\nUse 10.\n\nThis is called the scope chain.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "RjaTkbA8iPdm_NNZJgJhI",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7272.109561152236,
      "y": 755.8727173318475,
      "width": 1959.1105446510799,
      "height": 325.4814814814814,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a5i",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 616744557,
      "version": 2878,
      "versionNonce": 1183962573,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1790447190914,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "The lexical environment isn't one single global thing. There is a global lexical environment, and new lexical environments are\ncreated for different scopes (such as function bodies and blocks).\n\nWhen you call any function then a function execution context is created for that call, along with the function's lexical\nenvironment where its local bindings are handled.\n\nand when the function execution ocntext is removed form the stack then if the Lexical Environment is no longer\nreachable → it becomes eligible for garbage collection.",
      "fontSize": 32.548148148148144,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "The lexical environment isn't one single global thing. There is a global lexical environment, and new lexical environments are created for different scopes (such as function bodies and blocks).\n\nWhen you call any function then a function execution context is created for that call, along with the function's lexical environment where its local bindings are handled.\n\nand when the function execution ocntext is removed form the stack then if the Lexical Environment is no longer reachable → it becomes eligible for garbage collection.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "Qf0MWHhvq2_jSQXEODQOc",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 8596.680445612725,
      "y": 305.7461821462697,
      "width": 678.3326788163822,
      "height": 406.85185185185173,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a5j",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 876176772,
      "version": 2984,
      "versionNonce": 841129251,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790446288224,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "scope chain\n \n Basically it like two --> one --> global\n\nnow it find a in the two (not find) then\ngo one step up (not find) then go one\nstep up it find it at the global scope and\nprint it. and this is how it works\n\n",
      "fontSize": 32.548148148148144,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "scope chain\n \n Basically it like two --> one --> global\n\nnow it find a in the two (not find) then go one step up (not find) then go one step up it find it at the global scope and print it. and this is how it works\n\n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "xSu31P4GkWAX3OCBkUn6q",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5432.762486772484,
      "y": 449.01190476190527,
      "width": 1433.0051851851817,
      "height": 227.49999999999972,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a5l",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 662334852,
      "version": 2075,
      "versionNonce": 95686285,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790445501099,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Now the answer is A B C why ?\n\nBecause first global execution start A print then when it call the test() we get\ntest in the call stack and global execution is paused then we get B and when\ntest() is finished then GE run again and we get C",
      "fontSize": 36.399999999999956,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Now the answer is A B C why ?\n\nBecause first global execution start A print then when it call the test() we get test in the call stack and global execution is paused then we get B and when test() is finished then GE run again and we get C",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
