    {
      "id": "9kcnP_mimL2o6DLBBA3hL",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 23909.96672069501,
      "y": -1996.0122515574058,
      "width": 1190.7081448238143,
      "height": 591.4999999999993,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b10",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 693463044,
      "version": 5807,
      "versionNonce": 146331469,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "95Z3emARVaFShZ4WHQPNS",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1790445501102,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "The main thread and worker don't directly share normal JavaScript\nvariables. You will commonly see: self.onmessage and\nself.postMessage() self refers to the worker's global environment.\nIn the browser's main thread you commonly have: window. while a\nWorker doesn't have the normal DOM window\n\nWorkers cannot directly manipulate the DOM. A worker cannot do:\ndocument.querySelector(\"#app\"); because it doesn't have access to\nthe DOM as it doesn't have: window.document like the main thread.\n\nThe worker gets a structured-cloned version of that data. so\nwhen we send any object from the main thread it is a deep copy of\nthat which gone both have there own objects",
      "fontSize": 36.399999999999956,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "The main thread and worker don't directly share normal JavaScript variables. You will commonly see: self.onmessage and self.postMessage() self refers to the worker's global environment. In the browser's main thread you commonly have: window. while a Worker doesn't have the normal DOM window\n\nWorkers cannot directly manipulate the DOM. A worker cannot do: document.querySelector(\"#app\"); because it doesn't have access to the DOM as it doesn't have: window.document like the main thread.\n\nThe worker gets a structured-cloned version of that data. so when we send any object from the main thread it is a deep copy of that which gone both have there own objects",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "EJKxTA3nJ13SegHYWaDSi",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 23914.63338736168,
      "y": -1386.0122515574058,
      "width": 1727.374811490483,
      "height": 181.99999999999977,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b11",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1375051268,
      "version": 5980,
      "versionNonce": 261776813,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "95Z3emARVaFShZ4WHQPNS",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1790445501102,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Transferable Objects : - There is an important optimization. Some objects can be transferred\ninstead of copied. For example: const buffer = new ArrayBuffer(1024);\nworker.postMessage(buffer, [buffer]); The second argument: [buffer] is the transfer list.\nThis is useful when dealing with large binary data.",
      "fontSize": 36.399999999999956,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Transferable Objects : - There is an important optimization. Some objects can be transferred instead of copied. For example: const buffer = new ArrayBuffer(1024); worker.postMessage(buffer, [buffer]); The second argument: [buffer] is the transfer list.\nThis is useful when dealing with large binary data.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "qDH2b90q_B8JJ-t1v-3p0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 23909.39529212358,
      "y": -1183.0122515574058,
      "width": 1727.374811490483,
      "height": 318.4999999999996,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b12",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1508436484,
      "version": 6069,
      "versionNonce": 808873539,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "95Z3emARVaFShZ4WHQPNS",
          "type": "arrow"
        },
        {
          "id": "RQMgwVc_EqRAJVazk6fr-",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1790445501139,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Dedicated Worker : - The worker we've been discussing is called a Dedicated Worker. It belongs\nto one particular page/script. Another page doesn't normally use that same dedicated worker.\nShared Worker :- can be connected to and used by multiple browsing contexts (different\nwindows/tabs/iframes) rather than simply \"multiple files.\"\nService Worker :- browser runs it in response to events like network requests, push, notifications,\netc. It is mainly used for caching, intercepting requests, offline functionality, and background web\nfeatures.",
      "fontSize": 36.399999999999956,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Dedicated Worker : - The worker we've been discussing is called a Dedicated Worker. It belongs to one particular page/script. Another page doesn't normally use that same dedicated worker.\nShared Worker :- can be connected to and used by multiple browsing contexts (different windows/tabs/iframes) rather than simply \"multiple files.\"\nService Worker :- browser runs it in response to events like network requests, push, notifications, etc. It is mainly used for caching, intercepting requests, offline functionality, and background web features.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
